The projector's golden fixture.

export.json is the catalog's export (db/export/library-export.sql) of the fixture
fillProjection writes (projection_fixture_test.go), and expected/ what
library-v2-from-catalog.py --projections-only --as-of 2026-10-06T12:00:00Z makes of
it in a tree that holds the records: each item's metadata.json, each person's
person.json, and in images.txt the images they wrote. To write them again:

  KATALOG_PROJECTION_FIXTURE=<dir> KATALOG_TEST_DATABASE_URL=... go test -run TestWriteTheProjectionFixture ./internal/library/
  cd <dir> && python3 <schemas>/tools/library-v2-from-catalog.py --export export.json --out tree \
      --projections-only --as-of 2026-10-06T12:00:00Z

then copy export.json, every metadata.json as <itemId>.metadata.json, every
person.json as <personId>.person.json, and the images' paths into images.txt.

../projection-kinds/ holds the schemas' cases of an image of several kinds, from their tools'
suite (test_images_of_several_kinds, schemas a08c78e): fake_export's film with its artwork of one
image's bytes as a poster and a backdrop, and as a thumb, a poster and a backdrop, each projected
by library-v2-from-catalog.py --projections-only --as-of 2026-10-06T12:00:00Z in a tree holding
the film's item.json; each case's export.json, its metadata.json and images.txt as above.
